# Nimble Agent Builder Rules

These rules apply when the `nimble-agent-builder` skill is active.

## Transport order

Use the registered Nimble MCP server first when it is authorized. Use the Nimble
CLI only when the MCP tool surface is missing a required capability, when the user
explicitly chooses shell-based workflows, or when a batch/script workflow requires
local file I/O. Ask before installing the CLI or requesting API-key setup.

Foreground -- available operations:

| Command | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| Nimble MCP agents-list or `nimble agent list --limit 100` | Search for existing agents |
| Nimble MCP agent-get or `nimble agent get --template-name` | Display schema before run |
| Nimble MCP agent-run or `nimble agent run --agent --params` | Interactive execution |
| Nimble MCP search or `nimble search` | Web search / discovery |

background subtasks -- long-running operations (generate -> poll -> publish):

| Command | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `nimble agent generate --agent-name --prompt --url` | Create or refine an agent |
| `nimble agent generate --from-agent --prompt` | Iterate on existing agent |
| `nimble agent get-generation --generation-id` | Poll generation status |
| `nimble agent publish --agent-name --version-id` | Publish a version |

Agent creation runs in a background subtask because generation takes 1-3 minutes.

## Update over generate -- always

When `nimble agent list --limit 100` finds an agent on the same domain -- even with missing fields or different scope -- update it via `nimble agent generate --from-agent`. Do NOT generate a new agent from scratch.

Only generate from scratch when the agent list returns zero matches for the target domain.

## Every background subtask prompt must include the CLI commands

Copy this block into every background subtask prompt:

```
CLI tools (use via Bash):
- `nimble agent list --limit 100`
- `nimble agent get --template-name <name>`
- `nimble agent run --agent <name> --params '{...}'`
- `nimble agent generate --agent-name <name> --prompt "<prompt>" --url "<url>"`
- `nimble agent generate --agent-name <name> --from-agent <name> --prompt "<prompt>"`
- `nimble agent get-generation --generation-id <id>`
- `nimble agent publish --agent-name <name> --version-id <id>`
- `nimble search --query "<query>"`

MCP equivalents for Cline installs:
| CLI command | MCP tool |
|---|---|
| nimble agent generate | Nimble MCP nimble_agents_generate |
| nimble agent get-generation | Nimble MCP nimble_agents_status |
| nimble agent publish | Nimble MCP nimble_agents_publish |

Prefer MCP for Cline installs. Use CLI only when needed. Never curl MCP endpoints.
```

## Do not substitute unrelated web tools for Nimble workflows

When this skill is actively building or validating Nimble agents, use Nimble MCP
tools or CLI commands for the web-data steps. Do not replace a failed Nimble
workflow with unrelated web fetch/search tools unless the user explicitly changes
the task away from Nimble.

## Never use WSA tools

Never call `nimble_find_search_agent`, `nimble_run_search_agent`, or `nimble_url_extract`.
